# ============================================================
# AOME CONSULTS — NETLIFY HEADERS
# CSP is in REPORT-ONLY mode: nothing is blocked yet, but every
# violation gets logged in the browser console so we can see exactly
# which domains the live site actually needs before we enforce it.
#
# HOW TO USE THIS:
# 1. Deploy this file as-is.
# 2. Open the live site in a browser, open DevTools → Console.
# 3. Click through every page AND complete a full test booking
#    (this is the only way to trigger the Flutterwave checkout script).
# 4. Any blocked resource logs a line like:
#      "Refused to load ... because it violates the following
#       Content Security Policy directive ..."
# 5. Send me that list — we'll add anything missing, then switch
#    Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only to plain Content-Security-Policy
#    to actually enforce it.
#
# REMEMBER TO UPDATE before going live:
#   - backend URL is already set to: https://aome-consults.onrender.com
#   - replace https://*.supabase.co if your project ref ever changes
# ============================================================

/*
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://checkout.flutterwave.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: https://*.supabase.co https://checkout.flutterwave.com; connect-src 'self' https://aome-consults.onrender.com https://*.supabase.co https://api.flutterwave.com; frame-src https://checkout.flutterwave.com; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'
